      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your group traveling through Singapore and Vietnam, the key is determining if their stops are true layovers or if they are exiting the airport. Singapore generally has generous transit rules, but Vietnam's regulations can be more strict, especially if they plan to leave the airport. I recommend checking the official immigration websites for the latest rules for both countries, paying close attention to whether the layover requires a formal entry stamp. This proactive verification will ensure a smooth, hassle-free experience for all twelve engineers.",
      "source": "target",
